{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1487227-science-unbound","id":1487227,"title":"Science Unbound","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T12:20:46-07:00","id":1487227,"title":"Science Unbound","content":"<i>Another one of my monstrosities... and yes, the monster mash will get finished one of these days this summer XD </i><br /> <br /> Electricity can\u2019t resurrect the dead. Bathing in chemical concoctions kills people; it doesn\u2019t turn them into laughing psychopaths. Gamma radiation doesn\u2019t do anything other than rip DNA to shreds, but in the Shadow, that doesn\u2019t exactly matter. Perception and symbolism create Essence; physics doesn't. Wherever urban legends whisper of science run amuck, werewolves find Chemical Creation. This twisted spirit looms over its victims, an androgynous spectacled figure with too many needle-sharp teeth in its grinning mouth. Six arms ending in ten-fingered hands scribble notes on clipboards and prod its subjects with vicious-looking scientific tools.<br /> <br /> Chemical Creation obsesses over the way science transforms people. It lurks anywhere researchers expose test subjects to new compounds and unknown energies. It delights in plucking lesser spirits out of their ecosystems and using them to catalyze mortal experiments. It is particularly drawn towards packs (usually, but not always Pure) who utilized Claimed as tools or conduct rites to warp the Flesh. Oddly, it is also drawn towards Deviants and the Conspiracies that hunt them. The few Infused aware of Chemical Creation\u2019s presence suspect this interest is more than academic. They whisper that Chemical Creation is a Progenitor in its own right, but it does not actively seek to create Deviants and cares little for systematizing its methods. In this warped way, it has successfully created more Renegades than most Progenitors.<br /> <br /> <b>Chemical Creation</b><br /> <i>Rank 4 Transformation Spirit</i><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 9 Finesse 12 Resistance 12<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 25<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +24<br /> <b>Defence:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 26<br /> <b>Size:</b> 7<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 19<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Rumours \u2022, Transformation \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast, Catalyze Claim*, Dement, Deviant Rejuvenation*, Emotional Aura, Mortal Mask, Rapture, Telekinesis<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Discorporiate, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Chemical Creation cannot stop an experiment in progress.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> A scientific paper where a researcher denounces their own findings and admits the harm their theories caused.<br /> <br /> <i>New Numen - Catalyze Claim (R):</i> By spending 5 Essence, Chemical Creation may use the Forge Claimed Dread Power (Werewolf: the Forsaken 2e p. 219). Unlike Idigim with this Dread Power, Chemical Creation may only use it to place a spirit inside a human, and it does not immediately create a new Claimed; the spirit must go through the normal Claim process. Chemical Creation is also limited in the types of spirits it can implant into humans, they must be related to scientific phenomena, such as disease or radiation spirits, or they must be spirits related to emotions.<br /> <i>New Numen - Deviant Rejuvenation:</i> Whenever a Deviant suffers a minor or medium Instability in the same scene as Chemical Creation, the spirit regains 1 Essence. Whenever they suffer a Major instability, Chemical Creation regains 3 Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T12:54:35-07:00","id":1487236,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I like it. Nice way to induce a crossover element without <i>requiring</i> said crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}